From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:37:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: offer Zink a cached memory type kept coherent by the
 driver

Without IO coherency (kbase on Mali-G615 here: the GPU doesn't snoop CPU
caches for these mappings), PanVK's host-visible memory is either coherent
and uncached, or cached and non-coherent. Zink only uses cached memory when
it is also coherent, so its staging and readback buffers get the uncached
type. GameNative's OpenGL path presents every frame by reading it back
through such a buffer: a 1280x960 frame was copied out of uncached memory,
15-20% of the game's main thread.

Add a fourth memory type, HOST_CACHED | HOST_COHERENT, after the existing
ones, whose coherency the driver maintains: allocations from it get a cached
CPU mapping and join a per-device list; before every submission the CPU
caches of all mapped ones are cleaned, and whenever GPU work is seen to
complete (kbase sync waits, which timeline waits and counter queries also
end in) they are cleaned and invalidated. Mapping starts from a clean and
invalidated range; unmapping cleans first. The list lock is held while the
cache ops run, so a mapping can't go away under them.

The cleaning before each submission costs in proportion to how much memory
is in the list. DXVK also picks this type, for many buffers, and Megabonk
dropped from 60 to 42 fps with it, so it is only offered when the engine is
Zink ("mesa zink"); PANVK_EMUL_COHERENT_CACHED=1/0 forces it on/off.

Jupiter Hell (OpenGL through Zink), default clocks: main menu 50.7 -> 59.7
fps (60 is the cap); in the first level no measurable change (13.4 vs 13.9
fps; there the GPU clock and the game's pacing limit it, not the copy).
Megabonk and Hades (DXVK) unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR
(cherry picked from commit 7a04dc5c1ddb431dfc7d3cb3b060ed3180d9f9f4)

Purpose: give Zink a HOST_CACHED|HOST_COHERENT memory type whose coherency the driver keeps with CPU cache maintenance (clean before each submission, clean+invalidate when GPU work is seen complete), so its staging/readback buffers aren't uncached; GameNative's OpenGL path reads every frame back through one. Offered only to engine "mesa zink" (DXVK also picks it and loses fps to the per-submit cleaning)
Upstream-commit: none (Mesa main has the same two host-visible types without IO coherency)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none of ours; applies on the full g615-v11-csf series
Validation test: cohtest (CPU reads after GPU fill, GPU copy after CPU write, 4 KiB-4 MiB, completion via vkQueueWaitIdle / vkWaitSemaphores / vkGetSemaphoreCounterValue polling): 0 stale / 0 missing words on the new type (the plain cached type without maintenance: millions); Jupiter Hell main menu 50.7 -> 59.7 fps at default clocks, first level unchanged (13.4 vs 13.9); Megabonk 60 fps (42 when forced on for DXVK); Hades x64Vk at 1255 MHz 173.3 vs 172.4 fps; drawbench 8/8, racetest, msrtss identical
